flowchart TD
    S[Candidate agent + topology + version] --> D{Can Far Away discover an already-running normal session?}
    D -- No --> X1[Experimental or Unsupported]
    D -- Yes --> O{Documented/stable observation of relevant events?}
    O -- No --> X2[Experimental or Unsupported]
    O -- Yes --> L{Can liveness + parallel session identity + restart rediscovery be preserved?}
    L -- No --> X3[Monitor only or Unsupported]
    L -- Yes --> R{Safe exact bounded response to active correlated request?}
    R -- No --> M[MONITOR]
    R -- Yes --> W{Does mechanism preserve normal workflow and current live authority?}
    W -- No --> X4[Special topology: Experimental / Monitor]
    W -- Yes --> I[INTERACTIVE]

    I --> P[Choose mechanism per port]
    M --> P
    P --> P1[1 Same live authority]
    P1 --> P2[2 Workflow preservation]
    P2 --> P3[3 Documented / stable]
    P3 --> P4[4 Exact request correlation]
    P4 --> P5[5 Reconnect semantics]
    P5 --> P6[6 Security clarity]
    P6 --> P7[7 Simplicity]

    ACP[ACP is preferred only when it satisfies these constraints; session/list or load/resume alone does not prove live attach]
    P --- ACP